WEBVTT

00:00:04.366 --> 00:00:07.356
<b><i>was</i>/<i>were</i> and could</b>

00:00:08.377 --> 00:00:10.995
Gordon <b>was</b> Jeremy’s business partner.

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:13.519
They <b>were</b> at his country house.

00:00:14.231 --> 00:00:16.452
They <b>could</b> hear a strange noise.

00:00:18.963 --> 00:00:20.963
She <b>wasn’t</b> at home last night.

00:00:21.861 --> 00:00:23.600
You <b>weren’t</b> very nice to her.

00:00:24.372 --> 00:00:25.257
I <b>couldn’t</b> sleep.

00:00:27.695 --> 00:00:31.232
<b>Were</b> you sick yesterday? When was he <b>born</b>?

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:33.900
<b>Could</b> you see anybody in the library?

00:00:37.143 --> 00:00:38.430
<b>regular verbs</b>

00:00:39.421 --> 00:00:43.541
I really <b>liked</b> the present. She <b>wanted</b> to be a doctor.

00:00:45.741 --> 00:00:50.797
She <b>didn’t enjoy</b> the concert. They <b>didn’t arrive</b> until very late.

00:00:52.887 --> 00:00:56.860
<b>Did</b> you <b>watch</b> the game last night? When <b>did</b> you <b>finish</b> the book?

00:01:00.376 --> 00:01:01.905
<b>irregular verbs</b>

00:01:02.442 --> 00:01:06.780
I <b>went</b> to Paris last summer. She <b>slept</b> on the sofa.

00:01:08.754 --> 00:01:13.068
He <b>didn’t come</b> home last night. They <b>didn’t hear</b> the music.

00:01:15.154 --> 00:01:19.766
<b>Did</b> you <b>speak</b> to your sister yesterday? Where <b>did you <b>have</b> lunch?